Package: effectzones
Title: Interpretive Background Zones for Estimates and Confidence Intervals
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Hercules", "Freitas", , "hercules.freitas@uerj.br", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A 'ggplot2' extension that draws interpretive background zones
    behind estimates and confidence intervals in forest plots, post-hoc
    contrast plots and coefficient plots. Two modes are provided:
    effect-size magnitude zones based on published benchmark sets (e.g.
    Cohen, 1988, <doi:10.4324/9780203771587>) and clinical relevance zones based on a
    minimal clinically important difference (Jaeschke, Singer and Guyatt,
    1989 <doi:10.1016/0197-2456(89)90005-6>). The package does not compute,
    classify or reinterpret inference; it only draws a background against
    which existing estimates and intervals are read.
